35,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, I found something important! If we rent a whole building, the bill is just one big number we can split evenly. But last time, separate rooms cost different amounts, which is confusing! All-in meals are also a bit tricky.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, that is exactly why I wanted to check. All-in rates can be unfair to light eaters, and separate rooms create confusion. A whole house seems more predictable, though we must account for the food costs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've been thinking about our time together. Last year, some of us barely saw each other during the day, but in a shared house, there was no place to go for a moment of peace. We need a balance.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Looking at the logistics, the ferry schedule is quite restrictive. If the last one leaves at 16:20, we effectively lose two full days to travel. A city destination would be far more efficient for our time.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found out that the inns have very strict mealtimes and we'd all be in one room on futons. Also, the houses only have one bathroom, and some people said the water gets cold.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, one bathroom sounds like a disaster! We'll be waiting forever! @Victoria, since separate rooms are confusing and all-in meals are unfair, renting a whole house and paying for food as we go seems the fairest, right?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, it is the most transparent method. If we rent the house as a single unit, the base cost is fixed and predictable. We can then simply split the food receipts based on actual consumption.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, that sounds fair. But @Daisuke, if the house only has one bathroom, we might feel too crowded. Maybe a town with a public bath would give us that necessary space and balance?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, a town would certainly be more efficient. The city's frequent trains mean we wouldn't waste time planning every move, unlike the spa valley where we'd be limited by hourly buses and early cut-offs.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm worried about the one bathroom. And the inn's one-room layout with futons... it might be hard to find a quiet spot. A city room with a door sounds much more... relaxing.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, I totally get it! No one wants to fight over the bathroom. But if we go to the city, will the rooms be separate again? I don't want anyone paying more just because of their room!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, we can avoid that by booking a large apartment or a suite with a flat rate for the entire unit. That way, the cost remains a single, predictable sum for the group to split.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, that's a great solution. A city apartment would give us a shared space to bond, but the surrounding town would allow us to step away for a bit when we need a breather. It sounds like the perfect balance.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, I agree. Beyond the balance of space, the city option eliminates the travel overhead. We avoid the restrictive ferry times and the stress of hourly buses, allowing us to actually enjoy the holiday rather than managing it.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think a city apartment sounds best. Having a door and not having to follow a strict meal schedule would make it much easier to... to actually relax. I'd feel a lot more comfortable with that.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"Yay! A big city apartment sounds like a win-win! We get to split one bill evenly so it's fair, and @Daisuke gets his door! I'm all for it! Does everyone else agree?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. A city apartment provides the financial predictability I seek through a single flat rate, while addressing the logistical and comfort concerns raised by the others. It is the most rational choice for the group.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree as well. It solves the problem of feeling too crowded while ensuring we don't drift apart like last year. It's the best way to keep our harmony and make sure everyone is happy.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. Minimizing the time spent on transit and scheduling is my priority, and the city option is the only one that doesn't waste our limited days. It is the most efficient choice for everyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree too. It sounds like the best way for everyone to be happy, and I think I could actually get some sleep there. I'm looking forward to it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
