60,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Wait! I just noticed the options! Option B says ""separate accommodation,"" but we wanted a big apartment to split the bill evenly! If we have separate rooms, we're back to the confusing money problem!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, you are right to be concerned. If Option B implies separate bookings, we risk the same financial inconsistency as last year. We must ensure we can book a single unit to keep the cost predictable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Victoria, if Option B means we are truly separate, we might end up like last year, where some of us didn't even meet between breakfast and dinner. I'm worried we'll lose our group connection.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, while I understand your concern, the ""separate accommodation"" in Option B is still far superior to the logistics of Option A. The ferry schedule for the island is far too restrictive.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm worried about Option C. The inn's one-room layout and strict mealtimes sounded stressful. Even if Option B is separate, having my own door and space is... really important for me to feel okay.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Toshio, but the money part is still scary! If we do Option B and the rooms cost different amounts, someone will end up paying too much. Can we just agree to split the total cost of Option B evenly?","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Sakura, splitting the total cost of all rooms evenly is a fair solution. It removes the unpredictability of individual room rates and ensures that the final bill is a single, shared sum, which is the most rational way to proceed.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Sakura, @Victoria, if we agree to split the costs and make a conscious effort to spend time together, Option B could work. It gives us the personal space we need without sacrificing our bond.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Sakura, @Victoria, if we agree to split the costs, the financial issue is solved. More importantly, Option B avoids the travel overhead of the island and the rigid schedules of the inn. It is the most time-efficient choice.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. If we can split the costs and have our own space, Option B seems the safest. I think I can handle the separate rooms if it means I have a place to be quiet.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, @Toshio, @Midori, @Daisuke, thank you for agreeing! If we all promise to split the total cost evenly, then Option B is perfect! It's fair, it's easy, and everyone gets to be happy! I'm voting for B!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria"",""Toshio"",""Midori"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. As long as we commit to splitting the total cost of the accommodation evenly, the financial unpredictability is removed. Option B is the most logical choice to satisfy everyone's needs. I vote for B.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree. By splitting the costs and making a point to gather for meals or evening walks, we can avoid the isolation of last year while still having our own space. I vote for B.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"The travel efficiency of Option B is unmatched. By avoiding the ferry's restrictive schedule and the inn's rigidity, we maximize our actual time off. With the cost issue resolved, it is the only logical choice. I vote for B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. Having my own space and a flexible schedule is what I need most to feel okay. If we're all happy with it, I'll vote for B too.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Sakura,,"Yay! We all agree! Option B it is, with a big promise to split the costs evenly so it's fair for everyone! I'm so excited for our city adventure! B for me!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I concur. With the agreement to split the total cost evenly, the financial risk is mitigated. Option B is the most balanced and rational decision for our group. My final vote is B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm so happy we found a way to make everyone feel comfortable. Let's make sure we plan some lovely group activities so we stay connected. My final vote is B.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The decision is clear. Option B minimizes the time wasted on transit and scheduling, which is my primary concern. Since the financial and social issues have been addressed, it is the most efficient choice. My final vote is B.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we could figure this out together. Having a place where I can really rest makes a big difference for me. My final vote is B.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
